---
title: Chocolate chip cookies
servings: 24
tags: [american, vegetarian]
cuisine: american
source: Adapted from Chocolate Chip Cookies in tdstein/recipes (MIT), https://github.com/tdstein/recipes/blob/main/recipes/Chocolate%20Chip%20Cookies.cook
---

Heat the oven to 350°F (175°C).

Whisk the @all-purpose flour{3%cup}, @cornstarch{1.5%tsp},
@baking powder{1/2%tsp} and @salt{1/2%tsp} together in a #large bowl{}.

Stir the @baking soda{1/2%tsp} into @water{1%tsp}(hot) in a #small bowl{} until
it dissolves.

Melt the @unsalted butter{1%cup}. In a #stand mixer{}, beat it with the
@dark brown sugar{3/4%cup}, @light brown sugar{1/2%cup} and
@granulated sugar{3/4%cup} until smooth.

Beat in the @eggs{2} and the @egg yolk{1}, then the @vanilla extract{2%tsp},
then the baking soda water.

On low speed, add the dry mix in a few goes, just until combined. Mix in the
@chocolate chips{2%cup}.

Roll the dough into balls and set them on a #baking sheet{}. Bake ~{8%minutes}
to 10 minutes, turning the sheet halfway through.

Move to a #cooling rack{}.
